# THE CLAIM LEDGER — the load-bearing sentences of the shared-&T ruling, hashed.
#
# WHY A HASH AND NOT A GREP. The old lint checked that the STRING
# `type.shared-ref.write-through-derived-ub` appeared in src/compiler/mlir_gen_fn.cpp.
# MEASURED: replace the 105-line settled-rule comment with the false DEFERRED
# bullet it was written to correct — "unsound until we can prove T has no interior
# mutability (UnsafeCell AND atomics, which are NOT UnsafeCell-wrapped in our
# stdlib)" — leave the rule-id string alone, and the lint exits 0. It fires only
# when the id is ALSO stripped, i.e. it checks a label, not a claim.
#
# WHY NARROW BLOCKS AND NOT THE WHOLE FILE. Hashing the whole comment makes every
# honest edit a re-bless, and a gate that fires on honest edits is a gate someone
# deletes — the same defect one level up. So only the CLAIM SENTENCES are
# delimited in the source with `@claim <id>` … `@endclaim`. Everything outside a
# block — cross-references, measurement notes, the reasons a thing is written
# down — stays free to improve without touching this file.
#
# WHAT A MISMATCH MEANS. Not "you did something wrong": a claim's wording may
# well need improving. It means NO READER CAN TELL A REWORDING FROM A REVERSAL,
# so the change has to be stated. Re-hash, put the new value here, and say in the
# commit message which claim moved and why. That is the entire cost, and it is
# paid once per claim edit rather than once per comment edit.
#
# HASH: sha256 of the block body with `//` markers stripped and all whitespace
# runs collapsed to one space, first 16 hex digits. Re-wrapping a paragraph to a
# different column is therefore FREE; changing a word is not.
#
# Regenerate a value with:
#   python3 tests/logos/shared_ref_ub_readers.py claims src/compiler/mlir_gen_fn.cpp
#
# FORMAT: `<claim id>\t<sha256-16>`
#
# ── WHAT EACH CLAIM CARRIES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# guard.freeze-gated              the attribute is gated on type_is_freeze, and
#                                 the predicate is conservative on unknowns.
#                                 THE CLAUSE THE DEFERRED BULLET GOT WRONG.
# history.deferred-bullet-was-false  the record of that wrong answer, kept so it
#                                 cannot be pasted back as a fresh caveat.
# rule.unsafecell-is-not-a-writer the attribute does NOT rest on "nobody can make
#                                 such a pointer" — the cast is legal on every
#                                 type and ships as a stdlib API.
# rule.derived-write-ub           the rule itself, with its exception.
# rule.loaded-pointer-exception   why the exception is not optional: without it
#                                 the rule condemns Rc/Arc::clone.
# rule.rustc-parity-not-divergence  it belongs in the SPEC, not DIVERGENCES.md.
# exposure.confined-to-unsafe     no SAFE program can reach the rule (measured).
# exposure.no-stdlib-instance     the hand audit of the laundering sites, stated
#                                 as evidence rather than as proof of absence.
# status.write-detection-unenforced  nothing detects the prohibited shape in user
#                                 code. Stated so the rule is not read as a check.
exposure.confined-to-unsafe	d060c27b43734cb9
exposure.no-stdlib-instance	8749498221e0b1ea
guard.freeze-gated	a7869c0710d500bb
history.deferred-bullet-was-false	4cfc2275410c4858
rule.derived-write-ub	e82f52fbdf310339
rule.loaded-pointer-exception	851fcb9130810790
rule.rustc-parity-not-divergence	d797bcdcf15304c9
rule.unsafecell-is-not-a-writer	eb5e4ad70f26956e
status.write-detection-unenforced	8f5a7d74849d5531
